Hi Maggie,

I would collect calibration data at or above ~1-2 minutes in that case. You aren't really getting any additional information by going to 1Hz. I've attached a plot of the variogram of the residuals up to 10 minutes and you can see how autocorrelated the location errors become as you approach 1Hz. At 1 minute sampling, you have around 50% autocorrelation in location error. At 1Hz sampling, you have 99% autocorrelation.

Best,
Chris

